# Allen Relation: FINISHES / FINISHED-BY
#
# FINISHES: A and B end at the same time, but A starts later.
#   A finishes B  iff  A.start > B.start and A.end = B.end
#
# FINISHED-BY: the symmetric inverse — B and A end together, B starts later.
#   B finished-by A  iff  B.start > A.start and B.end = A.end
#
# Legal patterns that trigger FINISHES:
#   "until the expiry of the agreement" applied to multiple obligations
#   two protocols both terminating on the same fixed date
#   "all obligations under both X and Y cease on [date]"
#   a specific annex expiring when the main agreement expires
#   "the quota year ends on 31 December" for multiple product categories
#
# Grounded example (en_contracts_seed3):
#   Fishing opportunities protocol [1990-05-03, 1992-05-02] FINISHES
#   provisional application period [earlier_start, 1992-05-02].
#   Both end on 2 May 1992; the fishing protocol starts later.

```catala
declaration scope AllenFinishes:
  input interval_a_start content date   # start of the later-starting period
  input interval_a_end content date     # end of the later-starting period
  input interval_b_start content date   # start of the earlier-starting period
  input interval_b_end content date     # end of the earlier-starting period
  output is_finishes content boolean    # A starts later but ends at same time as B
  output is_finished_by content boolean # B starts later but ends at same time as A
```

## FINISHES

A starts after B but they share the same end date.

```catala
scope AllenFinishes:
  date round down
  definition is_finishes equals
    (interval_a_start > interval_b_start) and
    (interval_a_end = interval_b_end)
```

## FINISHED-BY

B starts after A but they share the same end date.

```catala
scope AllenFinishes:
  definition is_finished_by equals
    (interval_b_start > interval_a_start) and
    (interval_b_end = interval_a_end)
```
